From 2aa5e747fa35058bb27e7f632839ddc2073710f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: testuser <mainta@example.test>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 02:49:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/11] fix(cli): honor --data-dir under ACP and run the local
 backend without a hub daemon

Fork patch 0006. `cline --acp` returned before the sandbox setup, so --data-dir
and CLINE_SANDBOX=1 had no effect: ACP read providers.json from
$HOME/.cline/data/settings, wrote state under $HOME/.cline, and every session
started a detached hub daemon (--port 25463) that outlived the ACP process.

- resolveAcpSandbox runs configureSandboxEnvironment for ACP, so every state
  path moves into the data dir as in --json mode.
- A sandboxed ACP session (a data dir or CLINE_SANDBOX=1) creates its core with
  forceLocalBackend: true and builds sandbox: true, so no hub daemon starts.
- Without a data dir or sandbox flag, ACP keeps the default backend.
